# 中频词汇 List04
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 中频词汇List04核心词汇

{{colleague}}{/ˈkɒliːɡ/}{同事}{She discussed the project with her colleagues.}}
{{colonial}}{/kəˈləʊniəl/}{殖民的；殖民地的}{The country gained independence from colonial rule.}}
{{combine}}{/kəmˈbaɪn/}{结合；联合}{The recipe combines traditional and modern flavors.}}
{{command}}{/kəˈmɑːnd/}{命令；掌握}{The general issued a command to retreat.}}
{{commentary}}{/ˈkɒməntri/}{评论；解说}{The sports commentary was both informative and entertaining.}}
{{commerce}}{/ˈkɒmɜːs/}{商业；贸易}{International commerce has grown rapidly in recent decades.}}
{{compact}}{/kəmˈpækt/}{紧凑的；契约}{The apartment is small but compact and well-designed.}}
{{companion}}{/kəmˈpæniən/}{同伴；伴侣}{The dog has been a loyal companion for years.}}
{{comparison}}{/kəmˈpærɪsn/}{比较；对比}{In comparison with last year, sales have improved.}}
{{compatible}}{/kəmˈpætəbl/}{兼容的；相配的}{The new software is compatible with older systems.}}
{{compel}}{/kəmˈpel/}{强迫；迫使}{The evidence compelled the jury to reach a guilty verdict.}}
{{complain}}{/kəmˈpleɪn/}{抱怨；投诉}{Customers often complain about poor service.}}
{{complement}}{/ˈkɒmplɪment/}{补充；补足}{The two approaches complement each other well.}}
{{comply}}{/kəmˈplaɪ/}{遵守；服从}{All employees must comply with company policies.}}
{{compose}}{/kəmˈpəʊz/}{组成；创作}{The committee is composed of experts from various fields.}}
{{compound}}{/ˈkɒmpaʊnd/}{化合物；复合的}{The chemical compound has various industrial uses.}}
{{comprise}}{/kəmˈpraɪz/}{包含；由...组成}{The team comprises scientists from five countries.}}
{{compromise}}{/ˈkɒmprəmaɪz/}{妥协；折中}{Both sides reached a compromise after lengthy negotiations.}}
{{conceive}}{/kənˈsiːv/}{构想；怀孕}{It is hard to conceive of a world without technology.}}
{{concentrate}}{/ˈkɒnsntreɪt/}{集中；专注}{She concentrated all her efforts on the exam.}}
{{conception}}{/kənˈsepʃn/}{概念；构想}{The conception of human rights has evolved over time.}}
{{concrete}}{/ˈkɒŋkriːt/}{具体的；混凝土}{We need concrete evidence, not just theories.}}
{{condemn}}{/kənˈdem/}{谴责；判刑}{The government condemned the terrorist attack.}}
{{conduct}}{/kənˈdʌkt/}{进行；引导}{The scientist conducted extensive research on the topic.}}
{{confine}}{/kənˈfaɪn/}{限制；禁闭}{The discussion was confined to the main topic.}}
{{conform}}{/kənˈfɔːm/}{遵守；符合}{All products must conform to safety standards.}}
{{confront}}{/kənˈfrʌnt/}{面对；对抗}{The country must confront its history of inequality.}}
{{conscience}}{/ˈkɒnʃəns/}{良心；道德心}{His conscience would not allow him to lie.}}
{{conscious}}{/ˈkɒnʃəs/}{有意识的；自觉的}{She made a conscious effort to eat healthier.}}
{{consensus}}{/kənˈsensəs/}{共识；一致意见}{The committee reached a consensus on the new policy.}}
